[2026-02-04T00:18:21.020Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Viewport Frustum Culling for Canvas Visualizations\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: performance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: perf_optimizer\n- **Generated**: 2/1/2026, 11:42:57 PM\n\n## Description\nImplement viewport-aware rendering in AdvancedNetworkGraph.tsx and related canvas components. Currently drawClusters() at line 104-139 renders ALL clusters every frame regardless of visibility. Add bounding box intersection tests to skip off-screen elements, and implement level-of-detail rendering that simplifies nodes at high zoom levels (skip labels, reduce circle detail).\n\n## Reasoning\nCanvas draws 1000+ elements even when only 50 are visible, wasting 95% of render cycles. Frustum culling is a standard game engine technique that typically yields 5-10x frame rate improvements. Combined with LOD, users will feel immediate smoothness during pan/zoom interactions.\n\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\n- **compact-ui-design**: Use `.claude/skills/compact-ui-design.md` for high-quality UI design references and patterns\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d184f0d2-244e-457f-8ea5-4627f2d647f1","uuid":"71728ee7-1406-4906-95fd-feb81ad02e23","isSynthetic":true}
