[2026-02-04T00:21:15.648Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01BJ3Les6rzKzXBFKHrkbYum","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. Here's a summary:\n\n## Implementation Summary: Viewport Frustum Culling for Canvas Visualizations\n\n### Changes Made to `src/components/report/visualizations/network/AdvancedNetworkGraph.tsx`\n\n**1. Added Viewport Culling Utilities (lines 103-176):**\n- `ViewportBounds` interface for tracking visible area in world coordinates\n- `getViewportBounds()` - Calculates viewport bounds accounting for zoom/pan with padding\n- `isCircleInViewport()` - AABB intersection test for nodes and clusters\n- `isEdgeInViewport()` - Cohen-Sutherland-style line segment test for edges\n- `getLevelOfDetail()` - Returns LOD level based on zoom (full/reduced/minimal)\n\n**2. Updated `RenderContext` interface:**\n- Added `viewportBounds: ViewportBounds` for passing culling bounds\n- Added `lod: 'full' | 'reduced' | 'minimal'` for level-of-detail control\n\n**3. Updated `drawClusters()` (lines 178-220):**\n- Skips clusters outside viewport using `isCircleInViewport()`\n- Skips cluster borders at minimal LOD\n- Only draws cluster labels at full LOD\n\n**4. Updated `drawEdge()` (lines 222-322):**\n- Skips edges outside viewport using `isEdgeInViewport()`\n- Reduces edge opacity at minimal LOD to declutter\n- Skips arrowheads at minimal LOD (unless edge is in path)\n- Returns boolean indicating if edge was drawn\n\n**5. Updated `drawNode()` (lines 324-442):**\n- Skips nodes outside viewport using `isCircleInViewport()` with expanded radius for glow/labels\n- Skips glow effects at minimal LOD (unless node is important)\n- Skips shadows at reduced/minimal LOD\n- Simplifies border drawing at minimal LOD\n- Skips pin indicators at minimal LOD\n- Skips labels at minimal LOD\n\n**6. Updated render loop (lines 577-600):**\n- Calculates viewport bounds and LOD at start of each frame\n- Passes both to RenderContext for use by drawing functions\n\n### Performance Impact\n\n- **Before**: All 1000+ elements rendered every frame regardless of visibility\n- **After**: Only visible elements are drawn, with simplified rendering at low zoom levels\n- Expected 5-10x frame rate improvement during pan/zoom interactions when only a fraction of the graph is visible"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":74320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d184f0d2-244e-457f-8ea5-4627f2d647f1","uuid":"33e51feb-ce75-4402-8b81-5dd45d1d2036"}
